  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2021) position from National Bank's own audited annual report \"Five Years Financial Summary\", taken from the FY2024 report. SOLO basis including the bank's Offshore Banking Unit — the table is headed \"NBL and Its Offshore Unit\" (\"NBPLC and Its Offshore Banking Units\" from FY2025), which is National Bank's standalone presentation, not a consolidation of subsidiaries. Total liabilities are calculated as total assets minus total shareholders' equity; the source table prints no total-liabilities line. Net interest income is calculated as interest income minus interest expenses. Classified loans are calculated as the reported NPL percentage applied to reported loans and advances, because the table gives the ratio but not the absolute figure. Note that the row this dataset maps to operating_profit is the bank's \"Profit before Tax and Provision\", so it is pre-provision operating profit; the table reports no profit-before-tax line, so profit_before_tax is not available for any year. The FY2021 annual report IS in the archive but its PDF is image-only — pdftotext recovers 0 to 386 lines and no table row survives — so this year comes from the FY2024 report's comparative column.",
